{
  "version": "culture-mappings-1",
  "notes": [
    "Every UI culture has a deliberate entry: family = its land family (frontage, courtyard, compound, ...); pack = the houses architecture pack its lots borrow; borrowed = a declared geometric borrowing (fantasy or modern) rather than a shared native pack; functionalProfile = what one lot holds (town, communal = one household per lot, institutional); architectureFamily = the architectural layout, declared independently of the land family. Not a lexical guess: strict mode rejects borrowing in the programme stage.",
    "Cultures added for the medieval/fantasy world (docs/CITY_CULTURES.md) each reuse an existing native pack; none invents a house recipe. communal = one household per lot (tents, igloos, family huts); town lets lineage compounds, plank houses, warrens and the grown ordu hold several.",
    "Modern styles borrow a pack for the lot envelopes only (the narrow party-wall row house, a compact house, a courtyard house); their buildings are raised by massing.rs. A regional style borrows its region pack, whose monument family builds its temples and mosques."
  ],
